target: mf log
summary: The history of operations, by log context (default: list)

!! Reference

```
The history of operations, by log context (default: list)

Usage: mf log [COMMAND]

Commands:
  list      Display the history, by log context
  contexts  List the log contexts with their counts and what undid them, newest first, reading no operation
  head      Print the id of the newest operation
  show      Show full details of one log context (a log context id, or HEAD for the newest operation's)
  undo      Undo a log context of your newest change still standing (none named: list them)
  redo      Take back the undos of a log context of the newest undo still standing (none named: list them)
  revert    Undo a log context — what was written inside it — or an operation, by writing its inverse
  rollback  Go back to a time: revert your changes since then (not the watcher's)
  prune     Permanently remove operations from the history (irreversible)
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help
```
